# react-patterns (Cursor)

## Core principles

Render is a pure function of props/state — derive values during render,
don't stash derived data in `useState`+`useEffect`. Side effects
(mutations, network calls, subscriptions) live in event handlers or
`useEffect`, never in the render body. Compose via `children`/render
props/component props — React has no inheritance model.

## Hooks discipline

Top-level only, never conditional. Clean up every subscription/interval/
listener. Use the functional updater form when new state depends on old.
Default to not memoizing — add `useMemo`/`useCallback` only when a
profiler or dependency chain proves it matters. Extract a custom hook only
once the same hook sequence appears in 2+ components.

## State location

One component only → local `useState`. Parent + a few descendants → lift
to nearest common ancestor. Distant branches, low-frequency reads (theme,
auth, locale) → Context. High-frequency shared updates → external store
(Zustand/Jotai/Redux Toolkit). Derived from a server → a server-state
library (TanStack Query/SWR/RSC fetch). Most pages need neither context nor
a global store — resist abstracting until duplicated lifting hurts.

## Server/Client components (RSC)

Server Components are the default, async, ship no JS for themselves.
Client Components opt in with `"use client"`. Server→Client: pass
serializable props/children. Client→Server: invoke Server Actions via
`<form action>` or event handlers. Never import a Server Component from a
Client Component file — compose via `children` instead.

## Suspense + error boundaries

Place Suspense boundaries close to the data, not at the route root, for
progressive reveal. Error boundaries catch render/lifecycle/constructor
errors in children — not event handlers or async code.

## Forms

Prefer React 19 form actions (`useActionState` + `<form action>`) for new
code. Use controlled inputs when the value drives other UI or needs
real-time validation. For multi-step/dynamic/cross-field forms, use a
library (React Hook Form, TanStack Form) rather than rolling your own.

## Data fetching

RSC `await fetch()` for per-request Next.js App Router data; TanStack
Query for client cache+mutations+invalidation; SWR for lightweight
client cache; SSE/WebSockets for real-time. Avoid `useEffect`+`fetch` for
application data — no cache, no retry, race conditions.

## Performance

`React.memo` only helps when a component re-renders often, with usually-
identical props, and an expensive render — otherwise it's pure overhead.
Split context by concern so an unrelated change doesn't re-render
consumers. Stable `key` props (database id, never array index). Virtualize
lists past ~50 non-trivial rows.

## Accessibility

Semantic HTML before `role` attributes. Every interactive element keyboard
reachable. Labels on every form input. Manage focus on route/modal
changes. Run `axe` in component tests.
